<title>BELGIUM: Winterthur to pay 4.0 bln bfr for Josi.</title>
<headline>Winterthur to pay 4.0 bln bfr for Josi.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Winterthur Insurance Co and Belgian Assurances Group Josi said on Monday Winterthur's Belgian unit  Winterthur-Europe Assurances (WEA) would pay four billion francs for a 97.85 percent stake in Josi.</p>
<p>A joint statement released in Brussels said WEA would buy the stake from Holding Groupe Josi and Belgian holding company Cobepa.</p>
<p>Holding Groupe Josi and Cobepa would reinvest three billion francs in WEA via a capital increase, taking 9.6 and 4.8 percent stakes respectively.</p>
</text>
